From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ts4-port <ts4-port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:05:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] core: read the arm64 virtual counter instead of
 clock_gettime; throttle the CP heartbeat

- Clock::host_tick_count_platform() called clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW) on
  every tick query. On aarch64 read cntvct_el0/cntfrq_el0 instead: a register
  read, same monotonic source, no vdso call. The guest polls the performance
  counter often enough that __kernel_clock_gettime was 30% of all cycles in a
  simpleperf profile.
- The command-processor idle heartbeat sampled steady_clock::now() on every spin
  iteration, which is the same vdso call in the hottest loop in the runtime.
  Sample it once per 512 spins instead.

Measured on device: still a locked 60 fps, renderer 0.42 ms, whole-process CPU
276% (was 396% at 14 fps before the page-protection and counter fixes).
---
 src/core/clock_posix.cpp           | 15 +++++++++++++++
 src/graphics/command_processor.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/clock_posix.cpp b/src/core/clock_posix.cpp
index 00f2382..4454226 100644
--- a/src/core/clock_posix.cpp
+++ b/src/core/clock_posix.cpp
@@ -43,6 +43,21 @@ uint64_t Clock::host_tick_count_platform() {
   // clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW) returns nanoseconds, which would be
   // inconsistent with the 24 MHz mach frequency and cause ~41x time acceleration.
   return mach_absolute_time();
+#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+  // The guest polls KeQueryPerformanceCounter heavily (a simpleperf profile of the cinematic put
+  // 30% of all cycles in __kernel_clock_gettime). The virtual counter is a register read, so this
+  // costs a couple of cycles instead of a vdso call, and it is the same monotonic source.
+  // host_tick_frequency_platform() reports 1 GHz (1 ns ticks), so convert from the counter rate.
+  uint64_t counter;
+  __asm__ __volatile__("mrs %0, cntvct_el0" : "=r"(counter));
+  static const uint64_t frequency = [] {
+    uint64_t value;
+    __asm__ __volatile__("mrs %0, cntfrq_el0" : "=r"(value));
+    return value ? value : 1;
+  }();
+  // Split the conversion so counter * 1e9 cannot overflow.
+  return (counter / frequency) * 1000000000ull +
+         (counter % frequency) * 1000000000ull / frequency;
 #else
   timespec tp;
   int error = clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, &tp);
